{
  "figures": {
    "replicon": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-context\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 250\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-context-t fig-context-d\"><title id=\"fig-context-t\">Replication contexts</title><desc id=\"fig-context-d\">The chromosome, a separate plasmid, and an organellar genome are distinct templates. Viral DNA may become an intracellular replicon during productive replication. All depend on their biological environment.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"15\" y=\"35\" width=\"315\" height=\"165\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"172.5\" y=\"122.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Bacterial cell</text><rect x=\"350\" y=\"35\" width=\"315\" height=\"165\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"507.5\" y=\"122.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Eukaryotic cell</text><circle cx=\"83\" cy=\"90\" r=\"30\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"83\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Chromosome</text><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"90\" r=\"14\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Plasmid</text><circle cx=\"415\" cy=\"90\" r=\"28\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"415\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Nucleus</text><ellipse cx=\"590\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"48\" ry=\"27\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\"/><circle cx=\"590\" cy=\"90\" r=\"13\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Organelle DNA</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Separate template ≠ biochemical independence</text></g></svg><figcaption>Replication contexts. The chromosome, a separate plasmid, and an organellar genome are distinct templates. Viral DNA may become an intracellular replicon during productive replication. All depend on their biological environment.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-context\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "plasmid-architecture": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-map\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 270\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-map-t fig-map-d\"><title id=\"fig-map-t\">Schematic plasmid map</title><desc id=\"fig-map-d\">A circular sequence map separates the vegetative replication origin from maintenance, accessory and optional transfer regions. Arcs indicate sequence intervals, not measured sizes.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"120\" r=\"77\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M340 43 A77 77 0 0 1 413 96\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M414 98 A77 77 0 0 1 368 192\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M365 193 A77 77 0 0 1 275 162\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M274 160 A77 77 0 0 1 300 54\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Plasmid</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">sequence map</text><path d=\"M390 60L465 35\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"470\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">oriV</text><path d=\"M412 150L465 165\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"470\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Partition / control</text><path d=\"M325 195L325 230\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"325\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Accessory region</text><path d=\"M270 110L160 80\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"155\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Optional oriT</text></g></svg><figcaption>Schematic plasmid map. A circular sequence map separates the vegetative replication origin from maintenance, accessory and optional transfer regions. Arcs indicate sequence intervals, not measured sizes.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-map\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "theta": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-theta\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 235\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-theta-t fig-theta-d\"><title id=\"fig-theta-t\">Theta replication geometry</title><desc id=\"fig-theta-d\">One circle gives a branched intermediate with three duplex paths between two junctions, then two daughter circles. The duplicated arcs are highlighted; the drawing traces duplex axes, not individual strands.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><circle cx=\"85\" cy=\"108\" r=\"48\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"183\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Parent</text><path d=\"M145 108L205 108M196.13005077220717 112.61779175541483L205 108L196.13005077220717 103.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M250 108Q330 -5 410 108Q330 221 250 108\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M250 108Q330 75 410 108\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M250 108Q330 -5 410 108\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"108\" r=\"5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><circle cx=\"410\" cy=\"108\" r=\"5\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Duplicated arcs</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Unreplicated arc</text><path d=\"M425 108L480 108M471.13005077220714 112.61779175541483L480 108L471.13005077220714 103.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"555\" cy=\"65\" r=\"33\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"555\" cy=\"151\" r=\"33\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"555\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Daughter circles</text></g></svg><figcaption>Theta replication geometry. One circle gives a branched intermediate with three duplex paths between two junctions, then two daughter circles. The duplicated arcs are highlighted; the drawing traces duplex axes, not individual strands.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-theta\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "theta-control": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-cole1\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 260\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-cole1-t fig-cole1-d\"><title id=\"fig-cole1-t\">ColE1 primer control</title><desc id=\"fig-cole1-d\">RNA II can establish an origin hybrid and become a primer. Antisense RNA I interferes before productive hybrid formation; Rop can facilitate the inhibitory interaction.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">RNA II</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">primer precursor</text><rect x=\"245\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">RNA–DNA</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">hybrid</text><rect x=\"470\" y=\"20\" width=\"190\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"565\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Processed primer</text><text x=\"565\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Pol I extension</text><path d=\"M210 50L245 50M236.13005077220717 54.61779175541483L245 50L236.13005077220717 45.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M435 50L470 50M461.13005077220714 54.61779175541483L470 50L461.13005077220714 45.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"145\" width=\"190\" height=\"55\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"177.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">RNA I ± Rop</text><path d=\"M115 145L115 112L227 112L227 64\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M218 64L236 64\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"380\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Inhibits productive hybrid formation</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Copy abundance rises → stronger negative feedback</text></g></svg><figcaption>ColE1 primer control. RNA II can establish an origin hybrid and become a primer. Antisense RNA I interferes before productive hybrid formation; Rop can facilitate the inhibitory interaction.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-cole1\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "rolling-circle": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-rolling\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 240\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-rolling-t fig-rolling-d\"><title id=\"fig-rolling-t\">Rolling-circle geometry</title><desc id=\"fig-rolling-d\">A single nick yields a 3′-OH for extension and a 5′ end associated with Rep in the representative model. Displacement produces a tail; the outgoing strand can be circularized and copied. Lines show individual strands schematically.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"100\" r=\"51\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M100 58A42 42 0 1 1 88 60\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"102\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Nick</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">5′</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"49\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">3′-OH</text><path d=\"M159 100L215 100M206.13005077220717 104.61779175541483L215 100L206.13005077220717 95.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"315\" cy=\"100\" r=\"52\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M315 58A42 42 0 1 1 275 113\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M275 113Q255 160 320 180T433 180\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"315\" y=\"23\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Extension around circle</text><text x=\"389\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Displaced strand</text><path d=\"M437 100L486 100M477.13005077220714 104.61779175541483L486 100L477.13005077220714 95.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"70\" r=\"30\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"70\" r=\"24\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"158\" r=\"30\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"117\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">ds circle</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">ss circle → ds</text></g></svg><figcaption>Rolling-circle geometry. A single nick yields a 3′-OH for extension and a 5′ end associated with Rep in the representative model. Displacement produces a tail; the outgoing strand can be circularized and copied. Lines show individual strands schematically.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-rolling\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "copy-number": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-feedback\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 270\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-feedback-t fig-feedback-d\"><title id=\"fig-feedback-t\">Negative feedback and steady copy number</title><desc id=\"fig-feedback-d\">Hypothetical local model: synthesis per copy falls as copy abundance increases. The crossing at 15 genome equivalents per cell marks the steady abundance when dilution rate is 0.30 per hour.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><path d=\"M90 220L625 220M616.1300507722071 224.61779175541483L625 220L616.1300507722071 215.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M90 220L90 18M94.61779175541483 26.869949227792844L90 18L85.38220824458517 26.86994922779284\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Genome equivalents per cell</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Rate (h⁻¹)</text><path d=\"M90 40L540 190\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M90 115L590 115\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M315 115L315 220\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"315\" cy=\"115\" r=\"5\" fill=\"var(--accent)\"/><text x=\"315\" y=\"239\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">15</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">0.60</text><text x=\"62\" y=\"119\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">0.30</text><text x=\"505\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Dilution μ</text><text x=\"450\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">k(n)</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"85\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Net gain</text><text x=\"435\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Net loss</text></g></svg><figcaption>Negative feedback and steady copy number. Hypothetical local model: synthesis per copy falls as copy abundance increases. The crossing at 15 genome equivalents per cell marks the steady abundance when dilution rate is 0.30 per hour.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-feedback\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "segregation": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-partition\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 245\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-partition-t fig-partition-d\"><title id=\"fig-partition-t\">Random segregation and physical copy units</title><desc id=\"fig-partition-d\">Four independent circles give a specified-daughter loss probability of 1/16. Two particles, each containing two genome copies, give 1/4 under independent random segregation. Equal genome equivalents need not imply equal stability.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"20\" width=\"310\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><rect x=\"350\" y=\"20\" width=\"310\" height=\"160\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Four independent particles</text><text x=\"505\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Two linked pairs</text><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"99\" r=\"15\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"145\" cy=\"99\" r=\"15\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"205\" cy=\"99\" r=\"15\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"255\" cy=\"99\" r=\"15\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"470\" cy=\"99\" r=\"19\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"489\" cy=\"99\" r=\"19\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"555\" cy=\"99\" r=\"19\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"574\" cy=\"99\" r=\"19\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">N = 4; P = 1/16</text><text x=\"505\" y=\"151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">N = 2; P = 1/4</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Same four genome equivalents; different independent particle count</text></g></svg><figcaption>Random segregation and physical copy units. Four independent circles give a specified-daughter loss probability of 1/16. Two particles, each containing two genome copies, give 1/4 under independent random segregation. Equal genome equivalents need not imply equal stability.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-partition\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "incompatibility": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-incompat\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 250\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-incompat-t fig-incompat-d\"><title id=\"fig-incompat-t\">Shared versus independent feedback</title><desc id=\"fig-incompat-d\">A shared controller responds to A+B and may fail to restore the rare identity. Separate control circuits can respond to each identity independently. This is a conceptual diagram, not a measured molecular network.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"15\" y=\"22\" width=\"310\" height=\"175\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><rect x=\"355\" y=\"22\" width=\"310\" height=\"175\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Shared control</text><text x=\"510\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Independent control</text><rect x=\"35\" y=\"70\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"85\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A</text><rect x=\"205\" y=\"70\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"255\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">B</text><rect x=\"95\" y=\"140\" width=\"150\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"170\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A+B sensor</text><path d=\"M85 112L140 140M130.0004146061563 140.09106015170212L140 140L134.19044221570985 131.86064877579338\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M255 112L200 140M205.80955778429015 131.86064877579338L200 140L209.9995853938437 140.09106015170212\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"375\" y=\"70\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"425\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A</text><rect x=\"545\" y=\"70\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"595\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">B</text><rect x=\"375\" y=\"140\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"425\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">A sensor</text><rect x=\"545\" y=\"140\" width=\"100\" height=\"42\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"595\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">B sensor</text><path d=\"M425 112L425 140M420.3822082445852 131.13005077220717L425 140L429.6177917554148 131.13005077220717\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M595 112L595 140M590.3822082445852 131.13005077220717L595 140L599.6177917554148 131.13005077220717\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Shared feedback does not guarantee joint inheritance</text></g></svg><figcaption>Shared versus independent feedback. A shared controller responds to A+B and may fail to restore the rare identity. Separate control circuits can respond to each identity independently. This is a conceptual diagram, not a measured molecular network.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-incompat\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "episomes": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-episome\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 230\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-episome-t fig-episome-d\"><title id=\"fig-episome-t\">Free and integrated genetic elements</title><desc id=\"fig-episome-d\">An element can be an independently replicating circle or become part of a chromosome. When integrated, its sequence can be copied as the chromosomal fork passes.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"115\" r=\"65\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"245\" cy=\"115\" r=\"24\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"/><text x=\"135\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Chromosome</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"155\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Free element</text><path d=\"M290 95L390 95M381.13005077220714 99.61779175541483L390 95L381.13005077220714 90.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M390 135L290 135M298.86994922779286 130.38220824458517L290 135L298.86994922779286 139.61779175541483\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Integration</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"157\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Excision</text><circle cx=\"535\" cy=\"115\" r=\"65\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M535 50A65 65 0 0 1 590 80\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"7\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"210\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Integrated element</text></g></svg><figcaption>Free and integrated genetic elements. An element can be an independently replicating circle or become part of a chromosome. When integrated, its sequence can be copied as the chromosomal fork passes.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-episome\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "mitochondria": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-mt-timing\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 280\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-mt-timing-t fig-mt-timing-d\"><title id=\"fig-mt-timing-t\">Mammalian mitochondrial replication: asynchronous initiation</title><desc id=\"fig-mt-timing-d\">The time line illustrates the hypothetical calculation in the teaching text. Heavy-strand synthesis starts first. Light-strand synthesis begins when OriL is exposed, and finishes later in this example.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><path d=\"M65 220L635 220M626.1300507722071 224.61779175541483L635 220L626.1300507722071 215.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"350\" y=\"260\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Time from OriH initiation (min)</text><path d=\"M65 215L65 226\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">0</text><path d=\"M190 215L190 226\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"190\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">10</text><path d=\"M315 215L315 226\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"315\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">20</text><path d=\"M440 215L440 226\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"440\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">30</text><path d=\"M590 215L590 226\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">42</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">New H strand</text><path d=\"M65 65L440 65\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M420 65L440 65M431.13005077220714 69.61779175541483L440 65L431.13005077220714 60.38220824458517\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"440\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">H complete</text><text x=\"315\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">OriL exposed</text><path d=\"M315 75L315 145\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M315 155L590 155\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M570 155L590 155M581.1300507722071 159.61779175541483L590 155L581.1300507722071 150.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">L complete</text><text x=\"315\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">New L strand</text></g></svg><figcaption>Mammalian mitochondrial replication: asynchronous initiation. The time line illustrates the hypothetical calculation in the teaching text. Heavy-strand synthesis starts first. Light-strand synthesis begins when OriL is exposed, and finishes later in this example.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-mt-timing\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "plastids": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-plastid\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 235\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-plastid-t fig-plastid-d\"><title id=\"fig-plastid-t\">Sequence map versus physical organellar DNA</title><desc id=\"fig-plastid-d\">A circular reference map does not establish a single circular physical conformation. Linear and branched molecules are possible; these drawings are simplified shapes, not measurements.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"115\" r=\"70\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M120 45A70 70 0 0 1 180 80\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M120 185A70 70 0 0 1 60 150\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"8\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Genome</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">map</text><text x=\"120\" y=\"215\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Repeated arcs in green</text><path d=\"M205 115L275 115M266.13005077220714 119.61779175541483L275 115L266.13005077220714 110.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M325 65L565 65\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M325 130L565 130M420 130L470 95M475 130L510 175\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"445\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Linear molecule</text><text x=\"445\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Branched molecule</text></g></svg><figcaption>Sequence map versus physical organellar DNA. A circular reference map does not establish a single circular physical conformation. Linear and branched molecules are possible; these drawings are simplified shapes, not measurements.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-plastid\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "viral": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-viral-modes\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 250\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-viral-modes-t fig-viral-modes-d\"><title id=\"fig-viral-modes-t\">Contrasting viral replicative forms</title><desc id=\"fig-viral-modes-d\">Lambda, phiX174 and adenovirus illustrate different starting templates and replication contexts. The arrows summarize DNA forms rather than experimental procedures.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><rect x=\"15\" y=\"15\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">λ: linear dsDNA</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"15\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Circular dsDNA</text><rect x=\"485\" y=\"15\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"575\" y=\"45\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Theta / concatemer</text><path d=\"M195 40L250 40M241.13005077220717 44.61779175541483L250 40L241.13005077220717 35.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M430 40L485 40M476.13005077220714 44.61779175541483L485 40L476.13005077220714 35.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"95\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">φX174: ssDNA</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"95\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Duplex form</text><rect x=\"485\" y=\"95\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"575\" y=\"125\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Displacement / ssDNA</text><path d=\"M195 120L250 120M241.13005077220717 124.61779175541483L250 120L241.13005077220717 115.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M430 120L485 120M476.13005077220714 124.61779175541483L485 120L476.13005077220714 115.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"15\" y=\"175\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"196\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Adenovirus:</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"214\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">linear dsDNA</text><rect x=\"250\" y=\"175\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Protein primer</text><rect x=\"485\" y=\"175\" width=\"180\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"var(--surface)\"/><text x=\"575\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">DNA extension</text><path d=\"M195 200L250 200M241.13005077220717 204.61779175541483L250 200L241.13005077220717 195.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M430 200L485 200M476.13005077220714 204.61779175541483L485 200L476.13005077220714 195.38220824458517\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g></svg><figcaption>Contrasting viral replicative forms. Lambda, phiX174 and adenovirus illustrate different starting templates and replication contexts. The arrows summarize DNA forms rather than experimental procedures.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-viral-modes\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>",
    "evidence": "<figure class=\"figure-panel\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" id=\"fig-gel\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 250\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"fig-gel-t fig-gel-d\"><title id=\"fig-gel-t\">Interpreting bubble and Y structures</title><desc id=\"fig-gel-d\">A fragment with an internal active origin may form a bubble; a fork passing through a fragment can generate a Y. Geometry alone must be combined with mapping and labeling.</desc><g font-family=\"Arial,sans-serif\"><text x=\"180\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Internal initiation</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Fork passage</text><path d=\"M35 125L100 125Q180 50 260 125L325 125M100 125Q180 200 260 125\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M355 125L455 125L620 55M455 125L620 195\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"  stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">Two diverging junctions</text><text x=\"500\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"currentColor\">One junction within fragment</text></g></svg><figcaption>Interpreting bubble and Y structures. A fragment with an internal active origin may form a bubble; a fork passing through a fragment can generate a Y. Geometry alone must be combined with mapping and labeling.</figcaption><button class=\"tool-btn diagram-zoom\" data-figure=\"fig-gel\" type=\"button\">⊕ Enlarge diagram</button></figure>"
